   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to the use of EQUAL program funds for adult care facilities",
    "basePrintNo": "S5346",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5346-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §461-s, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5346\n\nTITLE  OF BILL:  An act to amend the social services law, in relation to\nthe use of EQUAL program funds for adult care facilities\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo clarify that  EQUAL  funds  may  be  spent  for  qualifying  expenses\nincurred  at  any  time  during  the fiscal year of the applicable EQUAL\naward.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nWould amend subdivision 4 of section 461-s of the social  services  law,\nto  authorize  the  use of EQUAL funds for expenses incurred at any time\nduring the fiscal year for which the funds were  appropriated,  provided\nResident Council approval is obtained for the expenditure.  This section\nwould  also  delete  the existing prohibition on using EQUAL funding for\nretrospective expenses.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEQUAL funding often occurs late in  the  fiscal  year.  In  the  interim\nbetween  award  and  the receipt of funding, operators often cannot wait\nuntil the actual issuance of  the  EQUAL  funds  to  purchase  items  or\nexecute  improvements  that  are the subject of the award. In such situ-\nations, the operator, with the resident council approval  --  should  be\nable  to apply the EQUAL funds retrospectively, to reimburse the already\npaid-for project.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
